; Every number below is an [Export] this screen hands to HomeLayout, and not one of them is decided
; in a script: a band height or a per-character budget baked into the renderer is a design decision
; hidden where no reviewer looks for it. The three band heights are the reference's 64 / 156 / 66
; logical at this canvas's 3x scale; the hero band is whatever is left.
;
; ⚠️ TopBarSidePadding is 24 rather than the reference's 36 (12 logical), and it is the one number
; on this list that deviates from the reference on purpose. The reference draws its settings glyph
; 30 logical wide and pads the bar 12; this build pads that glyph out to a 48-logical TAP TARGET,
; which takes 54 canvas units straight out of the pill row and leaves 684 where the reference has
; 738. At the longest values the brief itself names the three pills reserve 699, so the row was
; over-subscribed by 15 and the widest pill was drawn past the screen edge. The tap target may not
; move; four logical units of outer padding may.
[node name="Home" type="Node3D"]
script = ExtResource("1_home")
TopBarHeight = 192.0
LaunchHeight = 468.0
TabBarHeight = 198.0
TopBarSidePadding = 24.0
TopBarItemGap = 18.0
AvatarWidth = 108.0
SettingsGlyphWidth = 90.0
PillHorizontalPadding = 27.0
PillIconWidth = 48.0
PillInnerGap = 15.0
PillValueCharacterAdvance = 15.0
PillCaptionCharacterAdvance = 12.0
LaunchSidePadding = 42.0
LaunchRowGap = 30.0
StageCardHeight = 156.0
StartButtonHeight = 168.0
RewardLineHeight = 78.0
ChangeButtonWidth = 96.0
ChangeButtonHeight = 78.0

