; 🔴 The one line eleven destinations answer a tap with, and the twelfth thing on this screen that
; needed to exist: the tabs for Talents, Collection and Shop, the three rail entries, the settings
; control, the three resource pills and the refill offer all lead to screens this build has not
; written, and each of them used to answer a press by printing to the engine log. To the player that
; is a control that was tapped and did nothing, which is the definition of a dead button.
;
; It sits over the diorama rather than in a band of its own: a band would take height from the hero
; every frame for a line that is showing on almost none of them. HeroSubtitle for the same reason the
; two labels below it wear it — what is behind this is a picture, and an outline is the one contrast a
; flat font colour cannot give over one. Hidden until a tap asks for it, and it never takes a pointer:
; an acknowledgement that could itself be tapped is a control, and this is a sentence.
[node name="StubNotice" type="Label" parent="Ui/Screen/Bands/HeroBand"]
